/* {{BRAND_TITLE}} {{TITLE_WORD}} remote — global styles.
 *
 * CROSS-REPO PALETTE CONTRACT: every HugMesh-shaped UI reaches for the
 * --hug-* custom properties instead of pasting hex literals (contract source:
 * the host shell's styles.scss, mirrored from hugmesh.games; audit:
 * decisions/024-wcag-palette-audit.md). When this remote is mounted INSIDE the
 * host, the host's :root definitions win the cascade and theme this bundle;
 * the block below is the STANDALONE floor (ng serve / bare nginx) so the
 * remote is never unstyled on its own. Values match the host contract, each
 * with its contrast ratio against #0a0a12 recorded at the source.
 *
 * The --hug-* PREFIX IS LOAD-BEARING, not cosmetic — it is the name the host
 * shell's :root actually answers under, and the name every other remote in the
 * fleet is written against. A remote scaffolded onto any OTHER prefix still
 * LOOKS right STANDALONE (the literals below paint it) and so reads as working,
 * but once federated it resolves nothing from the host and stays frozen on this
 * block while the rest of the page rethemes around it. The Studio's injected
 * wire theme (snap-theme.css, :root:root) does still emit twins of every token
 * under the fleet's OLD prefix, but theme.py labels that a compatibility BRIDGE
 * for un-migrated repos — it is not the contract, and a repo born today has no
 * reason to be born needing it. */
:root {
  --hug-bg-0:        #0a0a12; /* shell + login backdrop */
  --hug-bg-1:        #12121e; /* cards, panels */
  --hug-bg-2:        #1a1a2e; /* scrollbar trough */
  --hug-border:      #1e1e32;
  --hug-text:        #e8e8f0; /* 15.9:1 AAA */
  --hug-text-muted:  #a8acc4; /*  8.77:1 AAA */
  --hug-accent:      #7c4dff; /* backgrounds/borders only — 3.22:1 as text */
  --hug-accent-soft: #b388ff; /*  7.38:1 AAA — use this for accent text */
  --hug-success:     #4caf50;
  --hug-error:       #ff6b6b;
}

html,
body {
  margin: 0;
  min-height: 100%;
  background: var(--hug-bg-0);
  color: var(--hug-text);
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
}
